  "verdict": {
    "findings": [
      {
        "gap": "The release addendum presents publishing main as sufficient to execute gh release create. It must require separate authority for the tag/release action; prior branch-push approval does not authorize it.",
        "risk": "An agent following this procedure can attempt a new remote publication without the action-bound PO decision required by the Operating Model.",
        "severity": "major",
        "evidence": "docs/push-release-flow.md:527-542",
        "spec_ref": "docs/operating-model.md:197-211"
      },
      {
        "gap": "Every source-release fixture substitutes a handwritten reader-checker stub. The passing case contains no reader records, while the stale case manufactures a failed result. The required real release CLI-to-checker integration remains untested.",
        "risk": "The green regression suite does not establish that the production checker launches successfully or that actual invalid, missing and stale records prevent an output artifact at the release entry point.",
        "severity": "major",
        "evidence": "plugins/pipeline-core/scripts/release-preflight-cli.test.mjs:54-71",
        "spec_ref": "specs/sprint-nova-epic/design/2026-09-10-current-candidate-artifact-audit.md:44-51"
      },
      {
        "gap": "The consumer approval commands use $REPO both to locate a Pipeline source checkout and to identify the application repository. A consumer installed through the documented plugin route lacks that plugins/pipeline-core path. Resolve the helper from the installed plugin root and pass the application root separately.",
        "risk": "The documented setup and approve-all commands fail in a normal consumer checkout; pointing $REPO at the Pipeline source instead targets the wrong repository.",
        "severity": "minor",
        "evidence": "SETUP.md:324-339",
        "spec_ref": "specs/sprint-nova-epic/design/2026-09-10-current-candidate-artifact-audit.md:23-25"
      },
      {
        "gap": "The German onboarding procedure still prescribes apply --activate. The current CLI has no flat apply command and rejects it; the supported action is apply-portable-seed with the reviewed plan digest.",
        "risk": "Following the advertised initializer stops with an argument error instead of initializing the consumer.",
        "severity": "minor",
        "evidence": "PIPELINE_FLOW.md:498-503",
        "spec_ref": "SETUP.md:118-127"
      }
    ],
    "deliberately_not_flagged": [
      "The inventory correctly remains pending with a null Critic receipt digest. This audit cannot supply publication attestation or replace the subsequent reader review.",
      "Reader binding intentionally proves committed-state equality and evidence presence, not reader identity or judgment quality. Those expressly excluded guarantees are not missing implementation.",
      "Both compatibility pins match the actual supplied preflight schema bytes. Synthetic reducer tests were not treated as evidence of live host compatibility.",
      "The seven submitted GG22 regressions invoke the real guard against Git fixtures and exercise the required pathspec distinctions. Existing guard implementation was not reopened for a general review.",
      "Missing historical dispatch evidence does not establish orchestrator authorship and was not converted into a lifecycle-violation finding."
    ],
    "trajectory_verdict": "not verifiable",
    "trajectory_evidence": "Requested route: openai / gpt-6-astra / max; effective provider/model identity is unverified. Closed-bootstrap ruleset: 4c9f2af31d5de30eddfd705664ca7e6cde38706e52a76805b19e2068f98c5d3c. Reviewed candidate: 8741613004e7ac84e48fa00a0a25e3d08ab682d1, tree 98e9803caac955aba2f8f8d4c568c93afff96f24; named tracked artifacts match those committed bytes. evidence/verify-1789018699972-53ebc75c368d86eb.json records node harness/scripts/verify.mjs on this clean candidate, with all 517 suites passing and no reused results. Verification execution is consistent, subject to the integration-coverage finding. scratch/NVA-CANDIDATE-REVIEW-COMPLETION-1/inventory-authorship-evidence.json explicitly lacks a supplied dispatch record and marks effective identity unverified; its Git metadata cannot establish production authorship. Observed context comprised the supplied AGENTS pointer, environment and host instructions; no session history was inspected. Persistence was unavailable under the no-write contract. Tests were inspected, not rerun.",
